INT. BRIDGE OF THE SURVEY SHIP PERIHELION - SHIP'S DAY

A circular room with a ceiling of living glass, its panes drifting from rose to amber as the star beyond brightens. Consoles ripple like water. Six stations, six people, one steady hum.

COMMANDER AOIFE BRANNIGAN, 50s, white hair cropped close, stands at the central rail with her hands behind her back. Dr. TENZIN LHAMO, 40s, sits at the spectrometer, scarf wrapped against the cold of the vacuum shield. RUKMINI SETH, 30s, pilot, long fingers on the helm sphere. JOSEF HALVORSEN, 60s, chief engineer, in a stained jumpsuit, taps a gauge. XIMENA TORRES, 20s, navigator, headset askew, twirls a pencil.

And the sixth is a voice that has no body: the ship's ORACLE.

ORACLE (V.O.)
(calm, genderless)
Perihelion in four minutes.

BRANNIGAN
Thank you, Oracle.

TENZIN
Spectral lines are doubling.

JOSEF
Hull plating's holding.

XIMENA
Helm, I'm showing a ripple at point two.

RUKMINI
I feel it.

ORACLE (V.O.)
Thermal shield at ninety-one percent.

BRANNIGAN
Josef?

JOSEF
Ninety-one is a good number.

TENZIN
(over Josef)
Commander, there's a signal in the corona.

XIMENA
(over Tenzin)
Pattern repeats every eleven seconds.

RUKMINI
(over Ximena)
It's not noise.

BRANNIGAN
Slow down. One at a time. Tenzin.

TENZIN
Eleven pulses, a pause, eleven pulses. Structured.

JOSEF
Stars don't count.

BRANNIGAN
Oracle. Source?

ORACLE (V.O.)
Source is within the corona. Origin: unknown. Analysis: a message.

Silence. The glass overhead turns from amber to a pale, searching gold.

XIMENA
What does it say?

ORACLE (V.O.)
Ximena Torres, it says your name.

Ximena drops her pencil. Brannigan does not move.

BRANNIGAN
Hold course. Hold shield. Everyone breathe.

RUKMINI
Holding.

JOSEF
Holding.

TENZIN
(softly)
Holding.

The signal pulses again. Eleven. A pause. Eleven.
